{"parentUuid":"2d8b475c-599b-4c53-b6b1-985b180a2767","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrACXSxuPx37VJyYsWb1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built two dry-run requests, so nothing was sent and nothing on the bucket changed. One request attaches the custom domain `uploads.demo.example` (zone `demo-zone`, TLS 1.2 minimum) to the bucket `demo-uploads`. The other sets a CORS rule that lets `https://app.demo.example` make `GET` and `HEAD` requests with a `Range` header, exposes `ETag`, `Content-Length`, `Content-Range` and `Content-Type`, and lets browsers cache the preflight check for one hour.\n\nBefore sending them, keep in mind:\n- **Everything becomes public.** Turning on the custom domain lets anyone read every object in the bucket at `uploads.demo.example`, not just your app. CORS only controls which browser pages can read the responses in script, so it doesn't restrict access. If the uploads are private, use signed URLs or a Worker in front of the bucket instead.\n- **CORS rules are replaced.** The CORS request overwrites the bucket's whole policy, and I didn't check what rules it has now. Any existing rules would be lost.\n- **No browser uploads.** I only allowed reads. If the app also uploads files from the browser, the rule needs `PUT`, `POST` and the matching request headers added."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":26931,"output_tokens":476,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":56},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1148,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":476,"cache_read_input_tokens":26931,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_inp